{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact S3 head 8230a6a21c54815b44c8c26690452856f5baafb0 on builder/state-s3-editor-20261107, tree 0d1ae47a, all 16 paths, for request 8ae87346 under promise a20e0cf1 and review request ac55e2fd. Each retained-editor stage now carries the evidence it needs, and one pure function makes every stage change. Every receipt check, context guard, original-request rule and message string from main stays. The gate at 4f4944ae failed, and it stays failed. The test-only follow-up meets the exception in docs/testing.md, for the reasons below.\n\nThe failed gate and the follow-up:\n\n- I read gate.exit at 4f4944ae, tree 9020c982: \"exit 1\". The typecheck step stopped in the lanes workspace's scope context (apps/room/lanes/tsconfig.scope.json). It reported nine errors, all in apps/room/lanes/test/directory-partition-editor.scope.test.ts, a caller of the old `task.state`, `task.steps` and `task.lane`. The other workspace contexts, including all three Page contexts, passed. No test phase ran. before.json and after.json are byte-equal, with lockfile 5a717d43 and gate.sh 001c4b10.\n- The repair dc073c3b changes only that test file and the note. No other file imports the test. The repair changes only how the test reads values: `task.state` becomes `task.stage.state`, `task.steps` becomes `task.stage.steps`, and `task.lane` becomes `editEvidence(task.stage).lane`. The case, its 15 assertions, their expected values and its 60-second deadline stay. `editEvidence` comes from production source that the failed gate already compiled and that has not changed since.\n- The follow-up ran the failed compiler context, then the whole test file (one case, passed), then `npm test`. All five test phases passed: Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 4,020 with one skip and Native 1,115 with two skips. The before and after records of both runs are byte-equal, and no owned process remained.\n- The follow-up did not run the ten root `tsc -p` projects that the typecheck step chains after the workspaces: scripts, apps/counter, apps/counter/browser, examples/lending, examples/lending/browser, examples/grow, apps/sandbox, examples/commons-bill, apps/views and examples/repo-in-ai. Their result is still established. Between M7's passing gate at 6da48104 and this gate's source, only apps/room/page files and notes change, and the repair adds only the lanes test. None of the ten projects includes or imports those files: apps/views and examples/repo-in-ai import only apps/room/lanes/src, which S3 does not change. So their compiler inputs are byte-identical to 6da48104, where the whole typecheck step passed. A future follow-up should run the remaining contexts of a failed step, or show this comparison itself.\n- After the repair, only the note and three manifests change. Merge 8230a6a2 brings in M7 main and keeps the tree of 7e865417.\n\nWhat else holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 01de2ca8 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 16 artifact paths: three Page source files, the generated Page module, four tests, the note and seven manifests. The commit-message check passes: 12 checked, 0 flagged. No dependency, lockfile, gate script, seal, grant, wire type or Wrangler file changes.\n- The Page module. GitHub reports run 42446009229 (Page browser scripts) as successful on the push of 4f4944ae, with every step successful. No apps/room/page file changes after 4f4944ae. The asset freshness test passed in the follow-up's plain phase.\n- The evidence. The seven manifests hash to the SHA-256 values that the note cites. Their 135 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The control disables only the receipt-verification refusal in `runStep`. The existing unverified-receipt case then fails by assertion: it reaches \"recorded\" instead of \"unknown\". Production source stays byte-equal.\n- The tests. retained-editor.test.ts (67), editor-list1.scope.test.ts (32) and directory-partition-editor.scope.test.ts (15) keep their number of `expect` calls, and every deadline stays. Each edited line changes only how a value is read. The deliberately corrupted task now sets its fields on `stage.previous`, where the Page reads them, so each check that hides \"Back to edit\" is still tested on its own. The new two-case test was committed at ff34db1a, when the editor source still matched main.\n- Semantics. An independent read of the three source files against main, with a probe of `transitionEdit`, found these preserved:\n  - the final stage and message for every event: sending, a refused or failed keep, a lost or timed-out answer, refused, archived, unavailable, mismatch, accepted but unverified, accepted and verified, a receipt read that throws, a context change, a check under the wrong room or key, and both the LIST1 and legacy paths;\n  - receipts: the task reaches \"recorded\" only after a verified step, and a step counts as verified only after `verifyStep` returns true, on the same signed bytes as main;\n  - the original request: every transition keeps the same frozen signed object, an unknown step settles only its original request, and the attempted step is recorded before the send, as on main;\n  - the guards in `taskRoom`, `prepareStep`, the opening read, the rules check, `verifiedCollectedSource` and the association check in `checkEditRequest`;\n  - every message string. Nothing is stored in either version, so no stored state needs a migration.\n\nThree visible differences are cosmetic:\n- The stage becomes \"unknown\" when the request is attempted, not when it fails. During the open-pr send, the Page therefore shows the \"Current file comparison is unavailable\" paragraph, which main hid until the send failed.\n- A refusal appears before the server's kept copy is ended.\n- A new \"lane-ready\" stage stores the lane and proposal once, from the first active lane, where main read them again on each Continue. The lane value cannot differ, because `followReceipt` checks the opening receipt's hash.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A stage can no longer hold a lane without its proposal, or a recorded state without its verified step. One function owns every transition and throws on one it does not allow. The network helpers return results and change no state.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The receipt rule, the association and context guards, and the original-request rule are unchanged. The Page still signs nothing new on a retry of an unknown step. One gap is older than S3: neither main nor this head tests the \"acceptance could not be verified; the task stays unknown\" branch in `checkEditRequest`. The transition function also trusts the controller's \"receipt-verified\" result.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Four notes:\n\n1. Each step stores `status` and also the old `attempted` and `receiptVerified` flags, two records of one fact.\n2. An earlier stage kept inside a later one holds an older `steps` list. Keeping `steps` on the task would remove that copy.\n3. If the \"receipt-verified\" result carried the entry it verified, `transitionEdit` could compare the signed bytes itself. The pure function would then own the receipt rule, and one test could cover the `checkEditRequest` branch.\n4. `readOpenedLane` reads the lane again on each Continue although the stage holds it, and `rulesReady` takes the lane from two sources.\n\nThis approval does not turn the failed gate at 4f4944ae into a pass. It authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb7ff6d9d789d4efae27c87683e3e27f024608ab","binding":"assigned","head":"8230a6a21c54815b44c8c26690452856f5baafb0","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:51d687cd5410ea2d1b08b2777cb8dec9eaa6d023\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c86a93f1488fb4797e5a95b6d77fe87a42c9381c\"]"